# API Handlers & Routes

> **Docs:** Every route must have complete OpenAPI metadata for Scalar (`/docs`). See `openapi-scalar-docs.mdc`.
> **Comments:** Handlers rely on OpenAPI descriptions; services/providers need JSDoc. See `code-comments.mdc`.

## Module Structure

Each feature lives in `apps/api/src/modules/{feature}/`:

```
{feature}/
├── {feature}.routes.ts    # Router — imports handlers, calls .openapi()
├── {feature}.metrics.ts   # Optional Prometheus counters (domain-specific)
├── handlers/              # One file per endpoint — route + handler colocated
├── services/              # Business logic (no HTTP concerns)
└── providers/             # External integrations (OAuth, etc.)
```

## Handler Pattern (Required)

Colocate `createRoute` and handler in the same file:

```typescript
import { createRoute, z } from "@hono/zod-openapi";
import { StatusCodes } from "@repo/config";
import { errorResponseSchemas } from "@repo/shared";
import { HTTPException } from "hono/http-exception";
import { type AppRouteHandler } from "@/types";

export const getResourceRoute = createRoute({
  method: "get",
  path: "/v1/resource/{id}",
  tags: ["Resource"],
  summary: "Get resource",
  request: {
    params: z.object({
      id: z.string().openapi({ param: { in: "path", name: "id" } }),
    }),
  },
  responses: {
    [StatusCodes.HTTP_200_OK]: {
      description: "Success",
      content: { "application/json": { schema: z.object({ message: z.string() }) } },
    },
    ...errorResponseSchemas,
  },
});

export type GetResourceRoute = typeof getResourceRoute;

export const getResourceHandler: AppRouteHandler<GetResourceRoute> = async (c) => {
  const { id } = c.req.valid("param");
  return c.json({ message: "ok" }, StatusCodes.HTTP_200_OK);
};
```

**Rules:**
- Use `AppRouteHandler<RouteType>` from `@/types` (not raw `RouteHandler`) for typed `c.get("user")` / `c.get("session")`.
- Export `export type XxxRoute = typeof xxxRoute` alongside the route.
- Validate input only via route schema — use `c.req.valid("param" | "query" | "json")`.
- JSON response shape: `{ message: string, payload?: T }` for success responses.

## Route Registration

Keep route files minimal — no business logic:

```typescript
import { createRouter, authRateLimiter } from "@repo/shared";
import { type AppBindings } from "@/types";
import { getResourceRoute, getResourceHandler } from "./handlers/get-resource.handler";

const router = createRouter<AppBindings>();
router.use(authRateLimiter); // when needed
router.openapi(getResourceRoute, getResourceHandler);
export default router;
```

Register in `apps/api/src/index.ts`: `app.route("/", featureRoutes)`.

## Auth Middleware

- `getUserMiddleware` — global; parses JWT, sets `c.var.user` / `c.var.session` (may be undefined).
- `enforceUserMiddleware` — route-level; throws 401 if no valid session.
- `enforceRoleMiddleware` — route-level; role checks after auth.

Protected handlers access: `const user = c.get("user")`.

## Rate Limiting

- `globalRateLimiter` — applied in `index.ts` (all routes).
- `authRateLimiter` — auth module routes.
- `strictRateLimiter` — sensitive operations.

## Services vs Handlers

- **Handlers:** HTTP validation, status codes, cookies, redirects.
- **Services** (`modules/{feature}/services/`): business logic, orchestration, token operations.
- **DB access:** via `@repo/db` service namespaces — never raw Drizzle in handlers.
